.TH NOSTR-HOME-STATUS 1 "2026-10-28" "nostr-homed 0.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nostr-home-status \- read porthome-status.json, manage quiet hours and quotas, resolve conflicts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nostr-home-status
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
[\fB\-\-field\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-quiet\-hours\-set\fR \fIHH:MM\-HH:MM\fR | \fBoff\fR]
[\fB\-\-path\fR]
.br
.B nostr-home-status quota
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
[\fB\-\-set\-override\fR \fIBYTES\fR | \fB\-\-clear\-override\fR]
[\fB\-\-reload\fR]
.br
.B nostr-home-status conflicts
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B nostr-home-status conflicts resolve
.I ID CHOICE
[\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR]
[\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Operator CLI over
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/nostr-homed/porthome-status.json .
The status file is a small JSON document written by three peers \(em
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8),
.BR nostr-home-fuse (8),
and
.BR nostr-homed-provision (1)
\(em each under its own top-level key (\fIsyncd\fR, \fIfuse\fR,
\fIprovisioner\fR).
.PP
Without arguments, prints the whole document pretty-printed. With
.B \-\-field
extracts a single scalar. With
.B \-\-quiet\-hours\-set
writes a config file consumed by the syncd throttle.
.PP
The
.B quota
subcommand reports (and, with
.BR \-\-set\-override / \-\-clear\-override ,
mutates) the syncd's per-user quota override.
.B \-\-reload
signals the daemon to re-read its configuration. It also shows the cache
and home sizes against their limits.
.PP
The
.B conflicts
subcommand lists unresolved conflicts from both the personal home
(\fIsyncd.home_conflicts\fR: sibling \fI.conflict-*\fR copies and deletion
markers) and shared folders (\fIsyncd.vault_conflicts\fR: copies under
\fIPortable/.conflicts/\fR, over-long names under
\fIPortable/.conflicts/.overflow/\fR, and deletion-only conflicts that have
no copy). Each entry has an ID, a plain-language explanation and the
choices available for it.
.PP
.B conflicts resolve
never edits files itself. It writes a request into
.B nostr-home-syncd (8)'s
inbox; syncd applies the choice and publishes it (a new personal-home
generation, or a new signed shared-folder head), then reports the outcome
in \fIsyncd.resolutions\fR, which the command waits for. The ID may be
abbreviated to any unique prefix of at least 6 characters.
.SH CHOICES
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-current
Keep what is at the original path now and discard the saved copy (for a
deletion conflict: keep the file).
.TP
.B \-\-use\-saved
Replace it with the saved version (for a deletion conflict: delete the
file).
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-both
Keep the current version and add the saved one beside it as
\fIname (conflicted copy ...)\fR. Not offered when one side is a deletion.
.TP
.BR \-\-keep\-mine ", " \-\-take\-theirs
Aliases that map to one of the above using the recorded provenance of
which version came from this device or account. Refused when that is not
known (for example, a shared-folder conflict between two other members).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the whole status document verbatim on stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-field \fIPATH\fR
Print one scalar. Dotted path syntax: the first segment is the writer name
(\fIsyncd\fR, \fIfuse\fR, \fIprovisioner\fR); the rest is a sub-key. Nested
lookup is best-effort, not full JSONPath.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet\-hours\-set \fIHH:MM\-HH:MM\fR
Write
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nostr-homed/quiet-hours
containing the range. Syncd honours the range on next scan tick.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet\-hours\-set off
Remove the quiet-hours config file.
.TP
.B \-\-path
Print the resolved status file path and exit.
.TP
.B quota \-\-set\-override \fIBYTES\fR
Persist a per-user quota override (in bytes) that overrides the default.
.TP
.B quota \-\-clear\-override
Remove the override; syncd falls back to the compiled default.
.TP
.B quota \-\-reload
Send SIGHUP to the running syncd (if any) so it re-reads the quota file
immediately.
.TP
.B conflicts \-\-json
List conflicts as a JSON array (id, source, path, saved_path,
saved_present, current_present, overflow, pending, mine, description,
choices).
.TP
.B conflicts resolve \-\-no\-wait
Queue the request and exit 3 without waiting for syncd.
.TP
.B conflicts resolve \-\-timeout \fISECONDS\fR
How long to wait for syncd's answer (default 30).
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT CODES
.RS
.TP 4
.B 0
Success.
.TP 4
.B 1
Malformed JSON or
.B \-\-field
matched no key.
.TP 4
.B 2
Bad argument.
.TP 4
.B 3
Status file does not exist; for
.BR "conflicts resolve" :
the choice was accepted but is not yet shared (offline, or no answer
from syncd before the timeout; a queued request is applied when syncd
runs).
.RE
.PP
For
.BR "conflicts resolve" ,
0 means resolved and shared, and 1 means syncd refused or failed the
request (the reason is printed).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/nostr-homed/porthome-status.json
Status document. Default state dir:
.IR ~/.local/state/nostr-homed .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nostr-homed/quiet-hours
Quiet-hours config.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nostr-homed/quota-override
Per-user quota override.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/nostr-homed/requests/
Conflict-resolution inbox read by
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8)
(mode 0700; one \fI<request-id>.json\fR per request).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Overrides the state directory root.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the config directory root.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nostr-homed-provision (1),
.BR nostr-homed-provision-status (1),
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8),
.BR nostr-home-fuse (8)
